Hi, everyone.

99
00:03:47,080 --> 00:03:48,120
I'm Jiang Shuying.

100
00:03:48,120 --> 00:03:49,040
You can call me Jiang.

101
00:03:49,920 --> 00:03:50,440
I've always been

102
00:03:50,440 --> 00:03:51,400
a loyal

103
00:03:51,400 --> 00:03:52,200
Heart Signal viewer.

104
00:03:52,200 --> 00:03:53,240
This time,

105
00:03:53,240 --> 00:03:53,880
I'm here

106
00:03:53,880 --> 00:03:54,560
as a Cupid

107
00:03:54,560 --> 00:03:55,880
to experience it with everyone.

108
00:03:55,880 --> 00:03:56,720
I can't wait to catch up.

109
00:03:57,360 --> 00:03:58,560
You should've been here sooner.

110
00:03:58,680 --> 00:03:59,640
I've been applying for ages.

111
00:03:59,640 --> 00:04:01,500
(Finally getting a close-up look)
They finally approved me this episode.

112
00:04:02,040 --> 00:04:02,560
What did you think

113
00:04:02,560 --> 00:04:04,120
of this season while watching it?

114
00:04:04,120 --> 00:04:05,520
Tell us about it.

115
00:04:05,520 --> 00:04:07,520
I watched until 2:30 last night.

116
00:04:07,840 --> 00:04:09,040
(I was really hooked)
I just couldn't stop watching

117
00:04:09,040 --> 00:04:09,920
Heart Signal.

118
00:04:09,920 --> 00:04:11,240
I was laughing and crying.

119
00:04:11,240 --> 00:04:12,360
It was so good!

120
00:04:12,720 --> 00:04:13,800
So Jiang,

121
00:04:13,800 --> 00:04:14,520
were there any other moments

122
00:04:14,520 --> 00:04:16,200
that really stood out to you
this season?

123
00:04:16,200 --> 00:04:17,520
Can you share some with us?

124
00:04:17,920 --> 00:04:20,880
Xing and Sun Bohan were out rowing.

125
00:04:20,880 --> 00:04:23,240
(Wu Xingying & Sun Bohan)
They said a star had fallen.

126
00:04:23,720 --> 00:04:24,880
Sun Bohan is such

127
00:04:24,880 --> 00:04:25,800
a cute guy.

128
00:04:25,800 --> 00:04:26,880
Whenever he talks to Xing,

129
00:04:26,880 --> 00:04:28,120
he keeps saying her name.

130
00:04:28,120 --> 00:04:29,520
He says her name all the time.

131
00:04:29,620 --> 00:04:30,720
Yeah, that's right.

132
00:04:30,720 --> 00:04:31,520
It's so cute.

133
00:04:31,520 --> 00:04:32,360
We noticed

134
00:04:32,360 --> 00:04:32,800
the same thing.

135
00:04:32,800 --> 00:04:33,080
Exactly.

136
00:04:33,080 --> 00:04:34,080
Who keeps saying the other person's

137
00:04:34,080 --> 00:04:34,880
name like that?

138
00:04:34,880 --> 00:04:35,920
Right. Not many people

139
00:04:35,920 --> 00:04:36,840
(Sun Bohan)
do that.

140
00:04:36,840 --> 00:04:37,800
He makes it

141
00:04:37,800 --> 00:04:38,880
(Sun Bohan's feelings are on display)
so obvious

142
00:04:38,880 --> 00:04:39,720
how much

143
00:04:39,720 --> 00:04:40,240
he likes her.

144
00:04:40,240 --> 00:04:40,960
Exactly.

145
00:04:41,120 --> 00:04:42,520
Whenever they are together,

146
00:04:42,520 --> 00:04:43,320
I can't stop smiling.

147
00:04:43,320 --> 00:04:44,200
I just can't help it.

148
00:04:44,200 --> 00:04:45,320
I was over the moon.

149
00:04:46,200 --> 00:04:46,600
Right.

150
00:04:46,600 --> 00:04:47,000
Exactly.

151
00:04:47,000 --> 00:04:47,760
And then there was Xiaoyu

152
00:04:47,760 --> 00:04:48,520
during the shout-out.

153
00:04:48,520 --> 00:04:49,680
Everyone was waiting

154
00:04:49,680 --> 00:04:50,920
for their chance

155
00:04:50,920 --> 00:04:51,760
to express their feelings.

156
00:04:51,760 --> 00:04:53,160
She stepped up to support her friend.

157
00:04:53,160 --> 00:04:53,640
She chose

158
00:04:53,640 --> 00:04:54,680
(Liang Xiaoyu supports her friend)
Meng.

159
00:04:54,680 --> 00:04:55,640
She chose friendship

160
00:04:55,640 --> 00:04:56,520
over love.

161
00:04:56,520 --> 00:04:57,280
She's a real one.

162
00:04:57,960 --> 00:04:59,020
After we finished filming
the last episode,

163
00:04:59,020 --> 00:04:59,540
I still hadn't had enough.

164
00:04:59,540 --> 00:05:00,480
(Please give us more)
I didn't want to leave.

165
00:05:00,480 --> 00:05:01,600
I couldn't sleep when I got home.

166
00:05:01,820 --> 00:05:03,060
(Second one to stay up late watching)
I was up past two.

167
00:05:03,440 --> 00:05:04,480
I just kept wondering

168
00:05:04,480 --> 00:05:06,560
who he'd ask to go rowing.

169
00:05:06,560 --> 00:05:07,780
(Every binge-watcher gets it)
What did that mean?

170
00:05:07,780 --> 00:05:09,200
- What did they mean?
- Why would they say something that harsh?

171
00:05:09,200 --> 00:05:09,760
Right?

172
00:05:09,760 --> 00:05:10,880
Who cried?

173
00:05:11,040 --> 00:05:11,920
Wasn't everything settled?

174
00:05:11,920 --> 00:05:13,320
How did we get another twist?

175
00:05:13,320 --> 00:05:13,960
Exactly.

176
00:05:14,040 --> 00:05:15,000
Hurry up and play it!

177
00:05:16,860 --> 00:05:20,420
(=Episode 5=
Write Your Name)

178
00:05:24,960 --> 00:05:27,040
They came back from the event.

179
00:05:27,040 --> 00:05:27,480
Yeah.

180
00:05:29,280 --> 00:05:30,280
You look like a greeter.

181
00:05:31,720 --> 00:05:33,020
Your hands just naturally

182
00:05:33,020 --> 00:05:34,060
(Mimicking)
go like this.

183
00:05:36,880 --> 00:05:38,000
I want to grill

184
00:05:38,000 --> 00:05:38,960
those chicken wings

185
00:05:38,960 --> 00:05:40,320
for a late-night snack.

186
00:05:40,320 --> 00:05:41,120
Sure.

187
00:05:42,320 --> 00:05:43,000
Hang on.

188
00:05:43,000 --> 00:05:44,080
Let me grab my menu.

189
00:05:44,420 --> 00:05:46,600
(Quick trot)
Love makes people cuter.

190
00:05:46,600 --> 00:05:47,400
Yeah.

191
00:05:50,640 --> 00:05:51,520
Liang Xiaoyu.

192
00:05:51,880 --> 00:05:53,880
Let's rest in our room for a bit.

193
00:06:00,680 --> 00:06:02,440
Let me have a Master Kong Jasmine Tea.

194
00:06:09,000 --> 00:06:09,600
Hi.

195
00:06:10,240 --> 00:06:11,180
You should massage for a bit too.

196
00:06:11,350 --> 00:06:12,330
I'll sit for a while.

197
00:06:12,460 --> 00:06:16,740
(Sits down)

198
00:06:17,170 --> 00:06:18,500
Relax and lie flat.

199
00:06:23,080 --> 00:06:24,640
Do you usually wear perfume?

200
00:06:24,660 --> 00:06:26,620
(Asking)
I never wear any.

201
00:06:26,640 --> 00:06:28,680
I guess I just never got
into the habit growing up.

202
00:06:31,840 --> 00:06:32,840
Are you guys cold?

203
00:06:34,000 --> 00:06:35,000
(Outside) It's freezing out there.

204
00:06:36,720 --> 00:06:37,560
Line up.

205
00:06:37,720 --> 00:06:38,720
Line up? Okay.

206
00:06:38,720 --> 00:06:39,760
Just lining up a few cups.

207
00:06:39,760 --> 00:06:40,720
You even understood that.

208
00:06:40,720 --> 00:06:41,480
I didn't understand you.

209
00:06:41,480 --> 00:06:42,320
(Glances)
You didn't reply.

210
00:06:42,320 --> 00:06:42,960
Why didn't I reply?

211
00:06:42,960 --> 00:06:44,040
It just happened to work out that way.

212
00:06:44,040 --> 00:06:44,720
Yeah.

213
00:06:45,800 --> 00:06:46,960
What temperature do you want your water?

214
00:06:47,720 --> 00:06:49,280
I can adjust it for you.

215
00:06:49,280 --> 00:06:50,360
That's so nice of you.

216
00:06:51,780 --> 00:06:52,700
(Cup won't open)

217
00:06:52,720 --> 00:06:53,520
You're still half-asleep.

218
00:06:54,080 --> 00:06:56,800
I just wanted to try a new method.

219
00:06:56,800 --> 00:06:57,600
Okay.

220
00:06:58,840 --> 00:07:00,280
Thanks for leaving
the class monitor to me.

221
00:07:00,280 --> 00:07:01,280
If it's the class monitor,

222
00:07:01,280 --> 00:07:02,640
(Glances)
we're probably

223
00:07:02,640 --> 00:07:03,120
screwed.

224
00:07:03,120 --> 00:07:04,000
The class monitor probably won't work.

225
00:07:05,320 --> 00:07:06,480
His mind's a mess.

226
00:07:07,960 --> 00:07:10,240
I might add some cold water.

227
00:07:10,240 --> 00:07:11,120
Be careful.

228
00:07:11,120 --> 00:07:11,440
Thanks.

229
00:07:11,440 --> 00:07:12,560
It's too hot.

230
00:07:12,560 --> 00:07:13,640
You can get your water first.

231
00:07:14,080 --> 00:07:15,280
I'm already done.

232
00:07:15,280 --> 00:07:16,080
You got it?

233
00:07:16,080 --> 00:07:17,140
(Clenches)

234
00:07:17,480 --> 00:07:19,840
When you said vice class monitor,
I had an idea.

235
00:07:20,040 --> 00:07:21,080
An idea.

236
00:07:21,080 --> 00:07:22,520
This idea should...

237
00:07:24,080 --> 00:07:25,640
Chen Hewen looks calm up top,

238
00:07:25,640 --> 00:07:27,000
but his feet are going wild

239
00:07:27,000 --> 00:07:29,520
underneath.

240
00:07:29,520 --> 00:07:30,780
(Chen Hewen)
Do you want some turmeric powder? Go.

241
00:07:30,800 --> 00:07:32,840
You've become more thoughtful.

242
00:07:34,000 --> 00:07:34,660
Really.

243
00:07:34,660 --> 00:07:36,420
(Rubs)

244
00:07:40,240 --> 00:07:41,000
Bye.

245
00:07:41,520 --> 00:07:42,640
See you guys.

246
00:07:45,820 --> 00:07:46,380
What should he do?

247
00:07:46,680 --> 00:07:47,800
He has no idea what to do.

248
00:07:59,320 --> 00:08:00,800
How did you feel about today?

249
00:08:03,120 --> 00:08:04,600
Standing all day made me a little tired.

250
00:08:04,600 --> 00:08:05,600
But it was actually pretty fun.

251
00:08:06,360 --> 00:08:07,480
Everyone was shouting back and forth.

252
00:08:07,480 --> 00:08:08,760
I really didn't expect that part.

253
00:08:09,040 --> 00:08:09,800
Then I was the first one to go up.

254
00:08:09,800 --> 00:08:11,000
I honestly didn't know what to shout,
but...

255
00:08:11,400 --> 00:08:12,640
I was the first one.

256
00:08:13,640 --> 00:08:14,360
I was the first one, right?

257
00:08:14,680 --> 00:08:16,440
But I was the first one
to shout out to you.

258
00:08:16,440 --> 00:08:18,120
(Liang Xiaoyu)

259
00:08:18,120 --> 00:08:19,120
Yeah.

260
00:08:19,560 --> 00:08:21,280
But I was the first one
to shout out to you.

261
00:08:21,720 --> 00:08:22,120
Yeah.

262
00:08:22,120 --> 00:08:23,880
You were the first one
to shout out to me.

263
00:08:23,880 --> 00:08:25,280
Chen Hewen.

264
00:08:26,840 --> 00:08:27,520
Yeah.

265
00:08:27,520 --> 00:08:28,720
To show everyone how it's done.

266
00:08:31,800 --> 00:08:33,040
I think Liang Xiaoyu

267
00:08:33,040 --> 00:08:33,960
is actually a very open

268
00:08:33,960 --> 00:08:34,760
and straightforward person.

269
00:08:34,760 --> 00:08:35,720
She's really direct.

270
00:08:36,120 --> 00:08:37,000
She's very easygoing.

271
00:08:37,120 --> 00:08:38,280
Very open and natural.

272
00:08:40,200 --> 00:08:41,640
I want to grill those chicken wings now.

273
00:08:41,640 --> 00:08:42,760
Otherwise,

274
00:08:42,760 --> 00:08:43,480
they might go bad.

275
00:08:44,120 --> 00:08:45,720
Regular parchment paper should work.

276
00:08:45,720 --> 00:08:46,240
Right?

277
00:08:46,240 --> 00:08:46,960
Yeah.

278
00:08:47,360 --> 00:08:48,760
Hello.

279
00:08:48,760 --> 00:08:50,000
I'm grilling chicken wings.

280
00:08:50,000 --> 00:08:50,560
You can try some later.

281
00:08:50,560 --> 00:08:51,840
You're so thoughtful.

282
00:08:52,000 --> 00:08:52,480
Here.

283
00:08:52,620 --> 00:08:54,580
(Offers)

284
00:08:56,240 --> 00:08:56,840
One?

285
00:08:56,840 --> 00:08:57,440
Two.

286
00:08:59,180 --> 00:09:00,980
(Helping)

287
00:09:09,440 --> 00:09:10,360
What temperature do you want your water?

288
00:09:14,760 --> 00:09:17,520
Just hot enough to drink. Hot is fine.

289
00:09:19,000 --> 00:09:20,480
Four hundred milliliters at 185°F,

290
00:09:20,480 --> 00:09:21,320
plus

291
00:09:21,320 --> 00:09:23,000
100 milliliters at 77°F.

292
00:09:23,000 --> 00:09:24,400
That makes it a little over 160°F.

293
00:09:25,480 --> 00:09:27,720
Sure.

294
00:09:27,720 --> 00:09:28,840
You decide.

295
00:09:31,520 --> 00:09:32,640
Sun Bohan, do you want some?

296
00:09:33,120 --> 00:09:33,560
Yeah.

297
00:09:33,800 --> 00:09:34,920
Make two cups.

298
00:09:35,280 --> 00:09:36,320
Two cups for who?

299
00:09:36,520 --> 00:09:37,560
You tell me. Who else?

300
00:09:39,120 --> 00:09:40,560
Who are the two for?

301
00:09:40,560 --> 00:09:42,280
It can only be for Xing.

302
00:09:43,720 --> 00:09:45,040
Yeah, that's right.

303
00:09:45,040 --> 00:09:46,880
I thought you meant two cups total
for everyone.

304
00:09:46,880 --> 00:09:47,600
Sorry.

305
00:09:47,600 --> 00:09:48,150
Thanks.

306
00:09:48,740 --> 00:09:51,220
(Smiles)

307
00:09:57,760 --> 00:09:58,880
What do you have to eat?

308
00:09:58,880 --> 00:09:59,240
What's this?

309
00:09:59,240 --> 00:10:00,520
I'm grilling chicken wings.

310
00:10:00,920 --> 00:10:01,840
Nice.

311
00:10:06,340 --> 00:10:07,420
(Observing)

312
00:10:07,440 --> 00:10:09,160
Why do you look so much thinner?

313
00:10:09,160 --> 00:10:10,400
I hate you.

314
00:10:10,680 --> 00:10:12,920
Did you secretly go on a diet
when you went home?

315
00:10:12,920 --> 00:10:13,560
No.

316
00:10:13,560 --> 00:10:14,360
Something's not right.

317
00:10:14,860 --> 00:10:16,320
(Stares)
Then I must've gotten fatter.

318
00:10:17,040 --> 00:10:18,700
(Explains)
It's the white. You're wearing white.

319
00:10:18,900 --> 00:10:20,080
White makes you look bigger.
Black makes you look slimmer.

320
00:10:20,080 --> 00:10:21,160
So you're saying I got fatter.

321
00:10:22,480 --> 00:10:23,440
Let's switch clothes.

322
00:10:27,820 --> 00:10:29,500
(Walks closer)

323
00:10:30,200 --> 00:10:32,280
Can you really stand not eating?

324
00:10:32,280 --> 00:10:32,920
Yeah.

325
00:10:35,240 --> 00:10:36,560
Then I won't eat either.

326
00:10:36,840 --> 00:10:38,760
Cui Kaiyi suddenly got all disciplined.

327
00:10:39,280 --> 00:10:40,480
Can you actually resist?

328
00:10:40,720 --> 00:10:41,920
I'm not sure I can.

329
00:10:43,820 --> 00:10:45,300
(Approaches)

330
00:10:45,780 --> 00:10:47,380
(Gets closer)

331
00:10:48,840 --> 00:10:49,640
Why are you laughing?

332
00:10:49,640 --> 00:10:51,400
I think I really did get fatter.

333
00:10:51,520 --> 00:10:52,080
No, you didn't.

334
00:10:52,640 --> 00:10:53,880
Look.

335
00:10:55,920 --> 00:10:57,160
Isn't it about the same?

336
00:10:58,540 --> 00:10:59,740
(Glances)

337
00:11:05,360 --> 00:11:08,240
Hello, everyone.

338
00:11:08,240 --> 00:11:09,360
I can't hold out.

339
00:11:09,360 --> 00:11:10,360
I'm cooking noodles right now.

340
00:11:10,360 --> 00:11:11,240
I really can't hold out.

341
00:11:12,720 --> 00:11:13,320
Guys,

342
00:11:13,320 --> 00:11:14,400
anyone

343
00:11:14,400 --> 00:11:15,600
want instant noodles?

344
00:11:15,920 --> 00:11:17,560
Anyone want some instant noodles?

345
00:11:18,320 --> 00:11:18,920
Who wants some?

346
00:11:18,920 --> 00:11:20,500
Sign up if you want some.

347
00:11:20,500 --> 00:11:21,260
(Joins immediately)

348
00:11:21,400 --> 00:11:22,440
She just said she wasn't going to eat.

349
00:11:22,440 --> 00:11:23,960
(Teeheehee)

350
00:11:23,960 --> 00:11:24,640
What am I gonna do?

351
00:11:24,640 --> 00:11:26,160
Starting tomorrow,
I'm not eating anymore.

352
00:11:26,640 --> 00:11:27,640
So cute.

353
00:11:29,160 --> 00:11:30,280
I'll learn.

354
00:11:31,080 --> 00:11:32,960
Learn how to cook instant noodles.

355
00:11:34,000 --> 00:11:35,920
They just want to spend time together.

356
00:11:37,720 --> 00:11:39,080
We can add

357
00:11:39,080 --> 00:11:39,600
whatever we want.

358
00:11:40,200 --> 00:11:41,560
Just wing it.

359
00:11:41,760 --> 00:11:42,520
You got this.

360
00:11:43,560 --> 00:11:44,200
We got this.

361
00:11:46,680 --> 00:11:48,240
We're basically not even trying

362
00:11:48,240 --> 00:11:48,920
to manage

363
00:11:48,920 --> 00:11:51,120
our image anymore.

364
00:11:51,680 --> 00:11:52,960
Well, you don't need to.

365
00:11:54,240 --> 00:11:55,520
You don't need to.

366
00:11:56,860 --> 00:11:58,460
(Watching the drama)

367
00:11:59,880 --> 00:12:02,040
Do you want some toast?

368
00:12:02,040 --> 00:12:02,840
Do you want some?

369
00:12:03,920 --> 00:12:04,640
Sure.

370
00:12:04,640 --> 00:12:05,400
Did you make it?

371
00:12:08,680 --> 00:12:09,480
Are you going

372
00:12:09,480 --> 00:12:10,580
to eat that bread today?

373
00:12:10,580 --> 00:12:11,180
(Learning)

374
00:12:19,760 --> 00:12:20,760
Do it again.

375
00:12:20,960 --> 00:12:22,160
Now I'm embarrassed.

376
00:12:22,160 --> 00:12:22,680
This...

377
00:12:22,680 --> 00:12:23,080
Don't.

378
00:12:23,080 --> 00:12:23,640
You...

379
00:12:23,640 --> 00:12:24,800
I'll show you next time.

380
00:12:25,600 --> 00:12:26,320
He's shy now.

381
00:12:32,720 --> 00:12:34,120
Do you need to stir it like that?

382
00:12:34,120 --> 00:12:36,800
Just trying to mix it with the noodles.

383
00:12:38,560 --> 00:12:39,640
How are you, Liang Renfang?

384
00:12:39,640 --> 00:12:41,080
Is your foot feeling better?

385
00:12:41,080 --> 00:12:42,280
It only hurts when I put weight

386
00:12:42,280 --> 00:12:43,520
on the front of it while walking.

387
00:12:43,620 --> 00:12:44,700
(Checking in)

388
00:12:44,920 --> 00:12:46,400
Yu Yang still feels guilty.

389
00:12:46,400 --> 00:12:47,600
Don't. Keep your voice down.

390
00:12:48,540 --> 00:12:49,600
(Feeling sorry)

391
00:12:49,640 --> 00:12:51,600
No, we're just talking.

392
00:12:52,200 --> 00:12:53,560
We're not blaming you.

393
00:12:53,560 --> 00:12:54,920
Yu Yang probably cried his eyes out.

394
00:13:01,760 --> 00:13:03,000
There's another one here. Try it.

395
00:13:03,560 --> 00:13:04,200
You...

396
00:13:04,200 --> 00:13:04,800
You guys eat it.

397
00:13:05,160 --> 00:13:05,680
We already ate.

398
00:13:09,920 --> 00:13:11,340
Look, I did this just now.

399
00:13:11,340 --> 00:13:11,920
(Opening it for him)

400
00:13:11,920 --> 00:13:12,480
This is so embarrassing.

401
00:13:12,480 --> 00:13:13,760
I even had to ask you to open it.

402
00:13:15,680 --> 00:13:16,480
How is it?

403
00:13:17,720 --> 00:13:19,040
Alright. I'm getting my nails done too.

404
00:13:21,600 --> 00:13:22,360
You can take some.

405
00:13:22,360 --> 00:13:23,480
I can't eat that much.

406
00:13:24,500 --> 00:13:26,460
(Handing it over)

407
00:13:27,480 --> 00:13:29,600
Yeah, just break off a piece for me.

408
00:13:29,600 --> 00:13:29,860
Yeah.

409
00:13:29,860 --> 00:13:30,920
(Breaking off a big piece)
I'll just try a little.

410
00:13:30,920 --> 00:13:32,080
No, I'll just eat this.

411
00:13:32,080 --> 00:13:32,760
- It's good.
- Okay.

412
00:13:38,160 --> 00:13:39,000
It should be done, right?

413
00:13:40,440 --> 00:13:41,240
Okay.

414
00:13:42,400 --> 00:13:43,960
What's wrong with this hand?

415
00:13:43,960 --> 00:13:45,080
This hand? It's cold.

416
00:13:45,080 --> 00:13:45,920
I thought

417
00:13:45,920 --> 00:13:46,840
it was gone.

418
00:13:47,600 --> 00:13:48,440
I'm "one-armed".

419
00:13:48,840 --> 00:13:49,640
Cutting off an arm to survive.

420
00:13:49,840 --> 00:13:50,680
(Looking)
It's cold.

421
00:13:50,680 --> 00:13:51,520
Cold.

422
00:13:51,800 --> 00:13:52,880
Sun Bohan, these chicken wings

423
00:13:52,880 --> 00:13:54,080
you grilled smell so good.

424
00:13:55,020 --> 00:13:56,460
(Checking in)

425
00:13:59,300 --> 00:14:00,500
(Glances)

426
00:14:03,580 --> 00:14:04,900
(Glancing)

427
00:14:04,920 --> 00:14:05,440
Where did you go?

428
00:14:06,320 --> 00:14:07,200
Here.

429
00:14:07,200 --> 00:14:07,480
You want?

430
00:14:07,480 --> 00:14:07,920
Thanks.

431
00:14:08,320 --> 00:14:09,200
Here.

432
00:14:09,200 --> 00:14:09,480
You want?

433
00:14:09,480 --> 00:14:09,840
Thanks.

434
00:14:09,900 --> 00:14:11,900
(Bringing Sun Bohan a blanket)

435
00:14:11,920 --> 00:14:12,680
Take a look.

436
00:14:14,860 --> 00:14:16,060
(Wiping hands)

437
00:14:16,080 --> 00:14:17,160
I was looking for you.

438
00:14:17,160 --> 00:14:18,240
Once you cover up with it,

439
00:14:18,240 --> 00:14:19,560
you warm up really fast.

440
00:14:19,560 --> 00:14:20,320
- Really?
- Super fast.

441
00:14:20,560 --> 00:14:21,240
Then let me see.

442
00:14:21,240 --> 00:14:22,120
Then I won't...

443
00:14:22,120 --> 00:14:23,120
Then I won't use this shirt.

444
00:14:23,860 --> 00:14:25,180
(Smiles)

445
00:14:25,760 --> 00:14:26,800
Then you're not "one-armed" anymore.

446
00:14:33,460 --> 00:14:34,780
(Smiles)

447
00:14:40,560 --> 00:14:42,480
There are actually
so many people in the kitchen.

448
00:14:43,880 --> 00:14:45,200
(Looking)
Meng.

449
00:14:45,200 --> 00:14:46,080
You can try some.

450
00:14:46,080 --> 00:14:46,480
Okay.

451
00:14:46,480 --> 00:14:47,880
I think there's one.

452
00:14:47,880 --> 00:14:48,320
I'll try it.

453
00:14:49,820 --> 00:14:50,860
(Looking for something)

454
00:14:50,880 --> 00:14:51,640
It's gone.

455
00:14:53,240 --> 00:14:54,160
Are you still going to eat?

456
00:14:54,480 --> 00:14:55,640
But I'm hungry.

457
00:14:55,640 --> 00:14:56,520
Then eat.

458
00:14:58,040 --> 00:14:59,680
Is something wrong?

459
00:14:59,680 --> 00:15:00,320
Who?

460
00:15:00,320 --> 00:15:01,080
You.

461
00:15:01,640 --> 00:15:02,400
No.

462
00:15:02,680 --> 00:15:03,280
Is it hot?

463
00:15:03,480 --> 00:15:04,040
It's okay.

464
00:15:04,040 --> 00:15:05,080
A little hot.

465
00:15:06,120 --> 00:15:06,840
It's fine.

466
00:15:07,480 --> 00:15:08,720
Add a little something.

467
00:15:09,380 --> 00:15:10,720
(Glances)

468
00:15:10,720 --> 00:15:12,280
What are you pulling out of your hand?

469
00:15:12,280 --> 00:15:12,920
Let me see.

470
00:15:13,440 --> 00:15:14,920
Meng looks so lonely.

471
00:15:14,920 --> 00:15:16,240
Everyone else has someone with them.

472
00:15:17,620 --> 00:15:20,060
(Walking away)

473
00:15:26,860 --> 00:15:29,580
(Leaving the kitchen)

474
00:15:33,520 --> 00:15:35,000
Yeah, it's daytime every day.

475
00:15:35,700 --> 00:15:37,300
(Glances)

476
00:15:44,560 --> 00:15:45,400
Feeling down.

477
00:15:46,040 --> 00:15:47,280
Meng, take a breather.

478
00:15:53,860 --> 00:15:57,580
(Sun Qimeng)

479
00:16:00,440 --> 00:16:02,160
I received

480
00:16:02,160 --> 00:16:03,680
a bouquet (The Courageous' flowers).

481
00:16:03,880 --> 00:16:04,480
Yeah.

482
00:16:04,720 --> 00:16:06,080
And I sent one too
(The Courageous' flowers).

483
00:16:06,800 --> 00:16:08,480
At dinner, I mentioned

484
00:16:08,480 --> 00:16:10,280
that my mood was white.

485
00:16:10,280 --> 00:16:12,360
When I first met you,

486
00:16:12,360 --> 00:16:14,000
you were wearing a white dress.

487
00:16:21,440 --> 00:16:22,960
It does take some time to process.

488
00:16:25,820 --> 00:16:27,020
(Wiping away tears)

489
00:16:27,040 --> 00:16:27,960
She's crying.

490
00:16:27,960 --> 00:16:29,960
She must be doubting herself.

491
00:16:34,080 --> 00:16:35,080
It's okay.

492
00:16:44,940 --> 00:16:48,020
(Sobbing)

493
00:17:26,120 --> 00:17:27,160
I really feel for her now.

494
00:17:27,760 --> 00:17:28,960
Sometimes,

495
00:17:28,960 --> 00:17:30,200
when you're feeling down,

496
00:17:30,200 --> 00:17:31,040
crying

497
00:17:31,440 --> 00:17:32,600
is just a way to let it all out.

498
00:17:32,600 --> 00:17:33,440
I think it's actually okay.

499
00:17:33,600 --> 00:17:36,080
(Cupid Dai Xu)
But she's eating while crying.

500
00:17:36,080 --> 00:17:36,960
I...

501
00:17:36,960 --> 00:17:38,440
I really can't handle seeing this.

502
00:17:39,000 --> 00:17:40,120
It makes it even more heartbreaking.

503
00:17:40,120 --> 00:17:40,800
She's keeping

504
00:17:40,800 --> 00:17:41,680
all that pain

505
00:17:41,680 --> 00:17:43,120
bottled up inside.

506
00:17:43,640 --> 00:17:45,320
But I think Meng has no regrets

507
00:17:45,320 --> 00:17:46,880
about this relationship either.

508
00:17:47,480 --> 00:17:48,280
She gave it everything she had.

509
00:17:48,280 --> 00:17:49,560
She used up all her courage.

510
00:17:51,720 --> 00:17:53,160
Why don't we go outside

511
00:17:53,160 --> 00:17:54,360
and take a walk?

512
00:17:54,360 --> 00:17:55,320
The second floor?

513
00:17:55,320 --> 00:17:56,080
Yeah.

514
00:17:58,080 --> 00:17:59,040
Meng's over there.

515
00:17:59,040 --> 00:17:59,800
She's alone.

516
00:18:00,450 --> 00:18:01,560
Maybe I should go check on her.

517
00:18:01,560 --> 00:18:02,080
Sure.

518
00:18:02,080 --> 00:18:02,600
Wait for me.

519
00:18:02,600 --> 00:18:02,960
Okay.

520
00:18:02,960 --> 00:18:03,760
Wait for me.

521
00:18:05,720 --> 00:18:06,920
She's her roommate?

522
00:18:06,920 --> 00:18:07,360
Yeah, her roommate.

523
00:18:07,360 --> 00:18:08,520
They're from the Courageous Room.

524
00:18:08,520 --> 00:18:09,780
(Sneaking quietly)

525
00:18:20,740 --> 00:18:23,060
(Crying out loud)

526
00:18:23,080 --> 00:18:23,520
What's wrong?

527
00:18:23,520 --> 00:18:24,320
Sometimes,

528
00:18:24,320 --> 00:18:26,520
being comforted just makes it harder.

529
00:18:26,520 --> 00:18:27,680
What's wrong?

530
00:18:27,680 --> 00:18:29,120
What's wrong, Meng?

531
00:18:29,120 --> 00:18:30,200
It's okay.

532
00:18:34,240 --> 00:18:35,440
Did something happen?

533
00:18:39,080 --> 00:18:40,280
I can't put it into words.

534
00:18:41,200 --> 00:18:42,800
Then you don't have to talk about it.

535
00:18:42,860 --> 00:18:45,100
(Comforting)

536
00:18:56,200 --> 00:18:57,600
Where did you just go?

537
00:18:57,600 --> 00:18:59,840
I was just eating ice cream.

538
00:19:01,360 --> 00:19:03,680
Why are you eating ice cream and crying?

539
00:19:03,680 --> 00:19:05,040
I needed some time to calm down.

540
00:19:05,100 --> 00:19:06,400
(Needed some time to calm down)

541
00:19:06,400 --> 00:19:07,320
Okay.

542
00:19:09,160 --> 00:19:10,920
Do you want to talk about it?

543
00:19:10,920 --> 00:19:11,880
Or

544
00:19:11,880 --> 00:19:13,520
you want to stay here
and eat for a while.

545
00:19:13,520 --> 00:19:15,280
I'll stay here and eat
for a while, okay?

546
00:19:15,280 --> 00:19:15,880
Okay.

547
00:19:15,880 --> 00:19:17,320
Don't tell anyone.

548
00:19:17,320 --> 00:19:18,600
I won't tell anyone.

549
00:19:19,040 --> 00:19:19,920
Then I'll go.

550
00:19:22,480 --> 00:19:23,440
Don't get cold, alright?

551
00:19:25,080 --> 00:19:26,040
Don't get cold.

552
00:19:26,540 --> 00:19:27,780
(Glances back)

553
00:19:29,100 --> 00:19:30,740
(Glances back again)

554
00:19:30,760 --> 00:19:32,040
Liang Xiaoyu is so sweet.

555
00:20:00,800 --> 00:20:01,680
What's wrong with her?

556
00:20:02,120 --> 00:20:04,200
She's a little sad.

557
00:20:04,200 --> 00:20:05,840
Shouldn't we

558
00:20:05,840 --> 00:20:06,800
comfort her a little?

559
00:20:06,800 --> 00:20:09,040
I asked her,
and she said she wanted to be alone.

560
00:20:10,160 --> 00:20:11,160
But usually, when someone says that,

561
00:20:11,160 --> 00:20:12,640
that's when you shouldn't
leave them alone.

562
00:20:14,520 --> 00:20:15,680
If you think I'm not the right person,

563
00:20:15,680 --> 00:20:16,920
why don't you go keep her company?

564
00:20:17,360 --> 00:20:18,560
I asked her

565
00:20:18,560 --> 00:20:19,800
if she wanted to talk to me.

566
00:20:20,600 --> 00:20:21,960
But she wanted

567
00:20:22,560 --> 00:20:24,160
to be alone for a while.

568
00:20:25,240 --> 00:20:26,680
Why don't we

569
00:20:26,680 --> 00:20:27,920
go out for a bit?

570
00:20:27,920 --> 00:20:29,240
I'll come back and check on her later.

571
00:20:29,240 --> 00:20:30,680
Okay. Sure.

572
00:20:31,360 --> 00:20:32,760
Let's give her some time.

573
00:20:32,760 --> 00:20:34,160
Since that's what she wants.

574
00:20:34,160 --> 00:20:34,840
Right.

575
00:20:34,840 --> 00:20:36,920
She needs time to process this.

576
00:20:40,160 --> 00:20:41,640
The last thing I wanted to see

577
00:20:42,200 --> 00:20:43,960
was something like this happening.

578
00:20:43,960 --> 00:20:44,800
It's not like

579
00:20:44,800 --> 00:20:45,400
you can just be funny

580
00:20:45,400 --> 00:20:46,400
or outgoing

